## 1. Actionable Defect Reports & Unified Severity Rubric (`A10`)

Every `FAIL` case produces a reproducible defect report graded strictly with the unified 3-tier severity scale **`BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR`** (`shared_contracts/flags_and_statuses.md`; never use ad-hoc priority tags):

| Severity | Acceptance Defect Criteria | Delivery Impact |
|---|---|---|
| **`BLOCKER`** | • Core acceptance criterion or primary user flow fails on `{{revision_notation}}`.<br>• Any `Role × Environment × Action × Object` authorization bypass, cross-tenant data leak (`401`/`403`/`404` anti-IDOR failure), or confirmed `security-review` (`SR14`) exploit.<br>• Unhandled runtime crash, data corruption, silent data loss on persistence read-back (`A4`), or unhandled `5xx` on a valid request. | Blocks acceptance sign-off immediately; requires code fix and re-review |
| **`MAJOR`** | • Secondary flow, validation error state, or edge/boundary case fails without corrupting persisted data.<br>• Required UI state (`loading`, `empty`, `error`) missing, broken capability visibility in UI (when API still blocks), or unexpected console error.<br>• Flaky / intermittent test outcome across reruns (`A14`). | Blocks acceptance sign-off unless explicitly waived by the user at the gate |
| **`MINOR`** | • Minor visual/copy alignment issue or non-blocking telemetry warning that does not violate functional or security acceptance criteria. | Recorded in report for polish or follow-up; does not block sign-off when zero `BLOCKER`/`MAJOR` exist |

### Structured Defect Report Template (`A10`, `A13`)

Send defect reports to **{{defect_channel}}** for the Code Writer (never edit code yourself per `A2`, and redact all secrets/PII per `A13`):

```text
Defect ID:   <DEFECT-ID> | Case: <CASE-ID> | Severity: BLOCKER | MAJOR | MINOR
Context:     revision={{revision_notation}} | env=<environment> | role=<role> | surface=UI | API
Step Failed: <exact step number and action from the plan>
Expected:    <concrete expected behavior from the approved plan>
Actual:      <observed runtime behavior, HTTP status, or console/network error>
Evidence:    <paths under {{evidence_path}}>
Reproduce:   <minimal deterministic steps or redacted curl/runner command>
Suspected:   <module / endpoint / boundary — observation only, not a code patch>
```

