## 2. Flakiness Classification Protocol (`A14`)

1. When a case fails unexpectedly, re-run the exact same steps **once** on the unchanged environment and revision (`{{revision_notation}}`).
2. If the case fails once and passes once (intermittent), classify the case as **`FAIL` (Flaky — `BLOCKER` or `MAJOR`)**, never `PASS`.
3. Attach evidence from **both** runs (the failing run and the passing rerun) so the Code Writer can diagnose the race condition, timing assumption, or shared-state pollution.

---

## 3. Re-Test Protocol After a Fix (`A12`)

When the Code Writer delivers a fix:
1. **Verify New Reviewed Revision (`A1`, `A12`)**: Confirm code review (and security review if applicable) approved the new git revision SHA (`<new-rev>`), and update the prepared test environment to `<new-rev>`.
2. **Execute Failed + Blast-Radius Cases (`A12`)**:
   - Re-run every previously `FAIL` or `BLOCKED` case on `<new-rev>`.
   - Re-run all regression and permission-matrix cases touching the modified files, endpoints, or shared components.
3. **Update Evidence Record (`A8`)**: Save fresh evidence bound to `<new-rev>` under `{{evidence_path}}` before handing results to {{quality_reporting_link}}.

---

## 4. Deterministic CLI Execution Gates (`PASS` / `FAIL`, `A14`)

All automated acceptance and smoke commands report strictly **`PASS`** or **`FAIL`** (`shared_contracts/flags_and_statuses.md`; `NOT_RUN`, `BLOCKED`, and `UNVERIFIED` never count as `PASS`):

| Gate | Command | `PASS` Criterion | `FAIL` Action |
|---|---|---|---|
| **G1 — Runtime Health & Revision Probe (`A1`, `A7`)** | `{{health_check_cmd}}` | Exit `0` — target service & revision live | Mark affected cases `BLOCKED` and halt execution |
| **G2 — Automated API & Permission Matrix Suite (`A6`, `SR14`)** | `{{api_acceptance_cmd}}` | Exit `0` — all contract, persistence & `401`/`403`/`404` tests pass | File `BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` defect with failing test output |
| **G3 — Automated UI / E2E Smoke Suite (`A5`, `A11`)** | `{{ui_e2e_cmd}}` | Exit `0` — all critical user flows and regressions pass | File defect with screenshot, trace, and console log |

